Source: https://github.com/OSRdesign/cyberdeck-zero-apps/tree/main/apps/mmwave-radar
Comment: The application is linked against the LVGL based cp0_lvgl runtime of the
 CardputerZero launcher by M5Stack (Copyright M5Stack Technology CO LTD, MIT) and LVGL
 (Copyright LVGL Kft, MIT), which are part of the binary and are therefore listed in
 its Copyright field below. The fonts it draws with are the launcher's; none is shipped
 in this package.
 .
 The frame decoder, the listen-only port detector, the tracker and the screen are the
 app's own code, written from scratch for this project from Hi-Link's published
 documents of the HLK-LD2450 serial protocol and the HLK-LD2452 user manual (facts of
 the data frame only) and from our own recordings of the sensor. It contains no code of
 other radar libraries. Hi-Link is named only to say which sensor the app reads; the
 project is not made, endorsed or sponsored by Hi-Link.
 .
 For a radar over Bluetooth LE the app talks to BlueZ over the system D-Bus with the
 sd-bus functions of the system's libsystemd.so.0 (systemd, LGPL-2.1-or-later), opened
 at run time: it is neither linked into the binary nor shipped in this package.

